// Package music ports Music (game/Music.ts, TSPS server commit
// bfd81e3): the Wiki's music areas, tile by tile, the area track
// lists, the random area-track pick, and the track lengths from
// DbTable 44.
//
// DATA PROVENANCE — READ BEFORE TOUCHING THE JSON: the area files
// (data/definitions/music-areas.json and
// data/definitions/music-areas-classic.json) are copied VERBATIM
// from upstream (server/data/definitions/ at commit bfd81e3).
// They were generated by scripts/import-music-areas.mjs. NEVER
// hand-edit them: fix the generator upstream and re-import. The
// modern file holds 612 areas and 2,012 plane-0 regions; the
// classic file holds 711 areas and 2,009 plane-0 regions.
//
// SCOPE: areas + track lookup + pick + lengths only. The
// per-session state machine that consumes them lives in
// internal/session (music.go); the song encoder lives in
// internal/protocol (song.go). NOT STARTED, all plugin-owned in
// TS: track unlocks (unlock bank/bit, autoUnlock, the
// "music:unlock-track" event), the "music:shuffle-track" pick,
// area getMusicTrack overrides, and jingles. instanceSourceTile
// (Music.ts, the templated-instance tile mapping) is not ported:
// no areas or instances exist in Go, so the session always feeds
// this package the owner's own tile.
//
// A nil *Data is the empty music state: TracksAt returns no
// tracks and LengthTicks reports no length, matching TS with
// empty areas and no cache lengths. The session layer relies on
// this when no music data was wired.
package music
